{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-02T09:17:15.200Z","author":"pi-glm","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"7687d94a08e852f40579b9f7","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-github-quay"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"SDK 2026.10.26 adoption: three real-SDK compensation tests fail on the pending toolchain PR"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Tracks gh:unbraind/pm-github#197 (filed 2026-10-29, missed by the blind issue watch). The open toolchain PR #194 (head 858cb976dc) resolves SDK 2026.10.26 and its test(22)/test(26)/bun-release(22)/(26) checks still fail (latest run 41330041504, 2026-11-01). Three real-SDK atomic-compensation cases (import-fidelity restoration after finalization; terminal-failure plan cleanup, fresh and recovery variants) receive 'compensation was incomplete' instead of completed compensation when an ordinary error is injected at committing; the suspected interaction is source-lifecycle finalization appending a Persistent import event inside the commit hook before the injected transition. Diagnose whether the host finalization contract or the test injection changed, fix, and keep the 100% thresholds."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["ci","gh:unbraind/pm-github#197","sdk-adoption"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-02T09:17:15.200Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-02T09:17:15.200Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"pi-glm"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6d