{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-03T09:27:51.980Z","author":"codex-toolchain-1103","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"9baccdd59fac06fda36f0bb8","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-03T09:27:51.980Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-03T09:27:51.980Z","author":"codex-toolchain-1103","text":"Reproduced the real-SDK compensation failure on the actual lockfile SDK 2026.10.28 (manifest remains >=2026.10.17). Root cause is the pm-cli 2026.10.26 GH-1591 ownership-proof hardening in src/sdk/item-transaction.ts. Before .26, compensateByRestore forced a timestamp restore. Since .26, hasOwnedCompensationEffects requires exclusive step ownership or a sibling compensation restoring the exact forward-state hash. commitGithubImportTransaction calls persistImportFidelity from its committing observer; that appends a separate import event (Preserve GitHub source lifecycle), so an ordinary subsequent observer failure correctly refuses rollback with transaction_partial_mutation rather than overwriting an unowned event. Classification: production integration depends on the former broad compensation behavior. Do not loosen the assertion or disable the SDK safety guard. Investigating a supported journaled finalizer; callback reordering or moving fidelity after commit would stop testing rollback after finalization and weaken the import guarantee."}]}],"before_hash":"61db7f75e7c7282331ade1d083f7786194aba14a8d4fd8a0242346ec6c01e289","after_hash":"efbe080f81e10c01f2f6eadead68126e78f2c432be69dda6773dbee3d20b87ee","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"stat